13
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:57,280
I like when big launches happen.

14
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:03,040
So, you know, admiring other people's big launches, I always want to make it, make the best launch possible.

15
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:05,280
So, yeah, the launch is very important to me.

16
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:06,960
Well, it definitely shows.

17
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:12,880
And the other thing that's come along with that waiting is I've become like a devoted Fantastic.

18
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:23,520
I was a person who didn't care that much about calendaring whenever I started this because I worked at a company and I sat in a room with all the people that I worked with.

19
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,960
And so yes, we had a calendar, but for the most part, you know, everybody would say, Oh, it's time for whatever.

20
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,960
